        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Is there a Normal mode? In [snacks.nvim#input](https://github.com/folke/snacks.nvim/blob/main/docs/input.md), `i_<Esc>` switches to Normal mode, while `n_<Esc>` cancels the input, similar to `CTRL-C`. I can't imagine using a custom input without this feature.\n\nThe [default key handler](https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-input.html#miniinput.default_key) emulates Command-line mode. It is possible to script on top of it, but it won't be a part of 'mini.input'. Mostly because Normal mode felt too out of place in this type of \"quick input\" scenarios when I was using plugins that had it (like 'telescope.nvim'). I can imagine wanting to use it, but without it the input is fully usable.",
