        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> In the help, `:h MiniInput.config`, there is a line that I don't understand:\n> \n> > It is also important to never change the current Neovim for |MiniInput.get()| to work as expected.\n> \n> Is this about detach/attach?\n\nIt was meant to be \"Neovim mode\". I'll adjust this.\n\n> Also, what is the intention of config.scope when the value is \"project\"?\n\nAs with any other value, it is up to the one who initiated the input. In general, it is usually the answer to the question \"The input for something related to the `scope` (cursor/line/.../editor/project)\". It was added mostly to follow the upstream documentation of `vim.ui.input` (current `master` but planned to be part of 0.12.3).",
