        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> One thing that I would wish for is something similar to Ctrl-f in cmdline mode, which opens up a separate buffer for editing. But after looking at the implementation I'm not sure if that can be done...\n\nYeah, I am afraid so. The very important point in 'mini.input' is that it does not change the mode and in the end returns the value. This is not *quite* possible (i.e. it might be done to a certain extent, but in a not very stable way) if input is taken through a regular buffer.",
            "created_at": "2026-06-09T09:54:10Z",
